  "de:226": "The Nigerian Catholic Church has long been a sanctuary of faith, and a guardian of moral values. Yet, beneath the grand cathedrals and the rhythmic chanting of the liturgy, a quiet crisis is unfolding. Our young people are looking across the street at their Pentecostal counterparts and seeing a starkly different reality—one where young voices […]",
